            "review_text": "kei\nParis, France19 contributions\n2\nA stylish Vietnamese restaurant. It's a lovely restaurant that looks like a neatly recreated old Vietnamese house.\nJan 2024 • Family\nI visited this restaurant because it was near my hotel and highly rated on Google Maps.\nIt was crowded with tourists (especially Koreans). I ate at a table on the first floor, but there was a tatami room in the back. There was a second floor, but it seemed closed because there was still space on the first floor.\n\nI think it was about 3,000 yen for three dishes (fried rice, fried spring rolls, and stewed chicken) plus a drink.\nThe roast pork that came with the fried rice was crispy on the outside and very juicy on the inside. The fried spring rolls were also really delicious, just as they looked in the photos.\n\nThere was a lot of food on the menu, and they gave me a menu in Chinese characters for Chinese tourists, but I had a hard time imagining the dishes.\nI regret not doing some research beforehand.\n\nAs with any restaurant in Nha Trang, the staff were very calm and reassuring.\nThe atmosphere of the restaurant was clean, and the plants outside were stylish. Couples and families can feel safe here!\nRead more\nShow original\nWritten January 13, 2024",
